items, and slot arguments. Preserve the slot-only duration conversion
retained by Bedrock 1.26.51.1. Historical engine query versions remain
outside the current licensed player bindings.

Evaluate bone-channel Molang this against the pose accumulated by earlier
tracks. The licensed crossbow graph uses -this to cancel holding offsets;
evaluating against channel defaults applied those offsets twice. Preserve
identity contributions for absent channels and reset context for authored
pose overrides. Verify crossbow charging, holding, and release through the
matching licensed graph. First-person playback and native visual
comparisons remain pending.

Supply active-stack food progress and trident brandishing inputs to the
licensed player graph. Native player getters divide startup from the
final 24 use ticks and drive a four-tick interval cycle. The target actor
update sets spear state only for an active Spear use animation with
remaining ticks, and clamps its charge over ten elapsed ticks. Keep
active-use stacks separate from equipped and rendered hands so stopping
use clears these variables. Match native floating-point operation order
and fast-use behavior with independent execution cases.

Native item duration differences, local predicted charging, first-person
playback, and visible native motion comparisons still need verification.

The Bedrock 1.26.51.1 charging query reads actor flag 43 independently of
item use. Publish accepted ViaBedrock player flags into immutable per-
connection snapshots for the licensed player graph. Read no mutable entity
metadata on the render thread, and retain replacement actors when an older
instance with the same UUID is removed. Independent execution verifies the
native query callback at FUN_142216b60; local predicted charging, other
specialized use states, and native visible motion remain separate work.

Native actor update FUN_142069380 supplies separate spyglass, goat-horn,
and brush states for carried use animations 10, 11, and 12. Resolve these
from the valid main-hand item and positive remaining ticks, independently
of the active-use stack. Keep food startup and interval progress on that
active stack, and calculate trident charge from the carried item duration.
The target Player main-hand getter reads its selected inventory slot at
FUN_140203320; these inputs must not follow Java off-hand use selection.

Independent execution verifies 364 combinations of carried and active
stack validity, target metadata, use animation, and remaining ticks, plus
different carried and active durations. Bind the named native variables
for authored classic tracks without synthesizing native item poses. The
extracted default player graph does not reference these three variables.
Full native item poses and post-use trident state remain separate work.

Acquire the matching vanilla sound banks, particle definitions, and atlases
