Play native collision-triggered child effects so the extracted water-drip
asset can produce its three rain-splash particles. Use the incoming speed
and final contact normal, dispatch before contact expiration, and preserve
the event frame and native event coordinates through child loading.
Support both block expiration predicates using original Bedrock identities
from the tracked primary palette, without an installed native client.

Independent execution of Bedrock 1.26.51.1 supplies 74 collision event cases,
16 event-coordinate cases and 64 block predicate cases. Collision probes
supply terrain, source callbacks and an identity frame template. Block
probes execute the native origin getter and membership lookup with a
prepared block set. Global startup, native registry name resolution,
complete child scheduling and visible comparisons remain unverified.
The production tests load the extracted drip and splash definitions;
licensed assets, binaries and research fixtures remain private.

Play emitter lifecycle and travel events through the bounded child graph.
The target creates events once on the first update, expires before origin
