and the target's vertical direction boundaries. Non-finite native axes
suppress that quad before Java vertex submission.

The owned 1.26.51.1 executable's facing name table and CPU quad builder
establish mode selection and orientation. Independent native instruction
execution covers 286 facing branch cases, 32 emitter basis cases, and 144
world-direction interpolation/normalization cases. These prepared probes
exclude camera selection, vertex submission, visible output, and complete
frame interpolation. The licensed package shaders receive finished vertices;
private shaders, executables, account licenses, and fixtures are not shipped.

Another 440 cases execute the native spin matrix multiplication after each
facing branch, with imported float32 cosf/sinf results supplied. Use the
resulting axes for both quad corners and frustum bounds so sheared planes
remain visible. Each frame owns its world direction and immutable matrix.

The owned Bedrock 1.26.51.1 actor-bound child factory starts with an
identity transform and binds the actor/locator separately. Preserve the
