collision rotation cannot rotate a bound child's locator a second time.
Native factory wrappers and the binding setter execute in 24 prepared
cases. Resource lookup, allocation/constructor, initialized matrix
constants, binding liveness, memcpy and cleanup boundaries are supplied;
actor query evaluation, branch selection and visible output remain outside
these fixtures. Add production comparisons and a scaled-locator regression.

Refresh particle actor query bindings before child initialization, updates,
and render expressions without sharing the parent's Molang variables.
Keep the target's generic particle animation clock fields separate from
actor animation time. Sample emitter camera distance from its cached origin,
and preserve native float32 velocity scaling in the ground-speed query.

The owned Bedrock 1.26.51.1 context refresh and initialization gate execute
in 54 prepared cases. Native scalar query callbacks execute with supplied
actor resolution, level access, variable storage, expression callbacks and
motion-component lookup. These cases establish query bindings and context
fields; live/offscreen actor updates, scheduling and visible playback still
need comparisons. Sample player queries during emotes as well as base poses.

The native actor-present child dispatcher passes the parent's base origin
as binding metadata while constructing the child at identity. Apply that
