FloatTag-only Hitboxes decoding, sorted endpoints and position-plus-pivot
recentered extents. The Discord capture has zero physical width/height and
a separate 1x2x1 picking box. Keep finite zero extents and restore physical
fallback only for an empty or rejected component.

Use the existing Java 26.3 picking predicates and block/reach clipping.
Proxy candidates inherit owner eligibility, root vehicle and inside-pick
rules. Current connection identity, generation and actor lifetime reject
stale updates. Local player proxies are rejected. Eighteen targeted core
and addon tests pass. Native radius callbacks, boundary clipping differences
and live joined NPC acceptance remain unverified; do not add guessed margins.

Negotiate actor_state_v3 alongside the byte-compatible v2 channel so native
UI consumers can resolve signed actor unique IDs to actual Java UUIDs.
Unknown v2 identities stay unknown rather than using runtime IDs as aliases.
The connection-owned registry preserves local player mapping and clears UID
associations on replacement, downgrade and disconnect. Bedrock 1.26.51.1
portrait consumer 148ddc410 resolves #entity_id through the Level UID lookup.
A targeted add-on lifecycle test covers local aliases, stale removal,
downgrade, upgrade and clear; the legacy decoder remains unchanged.

Bedrock 1.26.51.1 registers dynamic motion before parametric motion and
executes both callbacks. Its parametric update at 1461ca960 independently
overrides supplied position, velocity direction and rotation fields.
Omitted fields retain dynamic state. Direction retains speed except below
FLT_EPSILON; normalization rejects lengths below 0.0001. The licensed
executable SHA-256 is 537c0aee2e79afbdc94b44b28e00f466ae62bc50e2733d953b430db9dbaa9ee7.

Remove the exclusive-motion rejection reported for the CubeCraft
lightning trail. Do not add shape origin to an authored parametric
position or interpret its motion direction as billboard facing.
A mixed-motion emitter regression and 48 executed native constant cases
cover composition, independent overrides and the velocity thresholds.
Private native code and results remain outside the repository.
